==Trivia==
*Units in this version would display the first frame of their idle animation when knocked back, rather than having their own unique knockback sprites.
**Strangely, in [[The Battle Cats POP!]], [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]], [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]] and [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai]] all revert back to using this old iteration of the knockback animation.
*According to [https://www.kyoto-art.ac.jp/production/?p=52596 this blog post], this version was created when [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] only had nine employees, with only three of those employees even working on the game, forcing the art style and character designs to be very basic.
*[[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]] was the only stage to appear in both Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou and [[Kumanchu Royale]], albeit with different enemies in each game.
*The [https://youtu.be/g-ZTGRUMJrQ fifth music track] introduced in [[Zero Legends]] sounds similar to the original version of "Daichi Yurugasu Mosa-tachi" from Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou.

